doctype html
html(lang="en")
    head
        meta(charset="UTF-8")
        title User API Documentation
        style.
            body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; padding: 20px; line-height: 1.6; }
            h1, h2, h3 { color: #2c3e50; }
            pre { background: #ecf0f1; padding: 10px; border-radius: 5px; }
            code { background: #ecf0f1; padding: 2px 4px; border-radius: 3px; }

    body


        h1 User API Documentation
        p Base URL:
            strong #{baseUrl}/
        p
            | This API provides endpoints to manage user accounts, including signing up, logging in, validating JWT tokens, and deleting accounts.
            | Certain actions require authentication via JSON Web Token (JWT).

        h2 Authentication
        p
            | Some endpoints, specifically token validation and account deletion, require JWT authentication.
            | Include your token in the
            strong Authorization
            |  header:
        pre Authorization: Bearer &lt;your_jwt_token&gt;

        h2 Endpoints

        // --- Test JWT Token Validity ---
        h3 GET /user/test-token
        p
            | Validates the JWT token provided in the Authorization header. Useful for confirming whether a token is still valid and retrieving user information.
        p Example Request:
        pre
            code curl -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;your_jwt_token&gt;" #{baseUrl}/test-token
        p Example Response:
        pre
            code.
                {
                    "message": Token is valid!,
                    "user": {
                        "username": "admin123",
                        "email": "admin123@example.com",
                        "role": "admin",
                        "id": "68adc1d7f8d899baab44d774"
                    }
                }
        p Notes:
        ul
            li Returns HTTP 401 if the token is invalid or missing.
            li Returns HTTP 500 if there is an internal server error.

        // --- User Sign Up ---
        h3 POST /user/signup
        p
            | Allows a new user to create an account. Requires email or username and password.
        p Request Body (JSON):
        pre
            code.
                {
                  "username": "admin999",
                  "email": "admin999@example.com",
                  "password": "admin999",
                  "role": "admin"
                }
        p Example URL:
        pre
            code #{baseUrl}/user/signup
        p Example Response:
        pre
            code.
                {
                  "message": "Sign up successful",
                  "accountId": "68aef7cda84a59d1f373119d",
                  "token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
                }
        p Notes:
        ul
            li Returns HTTP 400 if required fields are missing.
            li Returns HTTP 409 if the username or email already exists.
            li Returns HTTP 500 on server error.

        // --- User Login ---
        h3 POST /user/login
        p
            | Authenticates an existing user using email or username and password. Returns a JWT token if successful.
        p Request Body (JSON):
        pre
            code.
                {
                  "username": "admin123",
                  "password": "admin123"
                }
        p Example URL:
        pre
            code #{baseUrl}/user/login
        p Example Response:
        pre
            code.
                {
                  "message": "Login successful",
                  "accountId": "68adc1d7f8d899baab44d774",
                  "token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
                }
        p Notes:
        ul
            li Returns HTTP 400 if required fields are missing.
            li Returns HTTP 404 if the account does not exist.
            li Returns HTTP 401 if the password is incorrect.
            li Returns HTTP 500 on server error.

        // --- Delete User Account ---
        h3 DELETE /user/delete/:id
        p
            | Deletes a user account by ID. Requires JWT authentication. Only the account owner or the default admin can delete an account.
        p Example Request:
        pre
            code curl -X DELETE -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;your_jwt_token&gt;" #{baseUrl}/delete/64e8d3f2a2b7b2a5c1f12345
        p Example Response:
        pre
            code.
                {
                  "message": "User account deleted successfully"
                }
        p Notes:
        ul
            li Returns HTTP 204 if deletion is successful.
            li Returns HTTP 403 if the user attempts to delete another account without admin privileges.
            li Returns HTTP 404 if the account ID does not exist.
            li Returns HTTP 500 on server error.

        h2 General Notes
        ul
            li JWT tokens are required for testing token validity and deleting accounts.
            li Passwords are securely hashed and are never returned in responses.
            li All responses include informative HTTP status codes and messages.
